window.docContents[134].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L0-___-The-black-box--Learning-path":{"contents":"* #* Do* Checked by HCP.L0_BlackBox anchor* Concept disclosed\n* 1* In the bare-real oscillator, write the reciprocal quotient under the square root.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#bare_reals* Bare reals do not distinguish the two formulas.\n* 2* Return the tagged potential energy at its declared dimension; inspect both quotient types and try the cross-assignment.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#potential_energy_dimension; HCP.L0_BlackBox#quotient_dimensions* WithDim accepts each quotient at its own dimension and rejects assigning m/k to k/m's type.\n* 3* Pass an angular-frequency value typed as WithDim T𝓭⁻¹ ℝ≥0 to a parameter typed as Frequency.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#frequency_alias* The alias accepts it because the dimensions and carrier types coincide; there is no kind distinction.\n* 4* Decide kind inequality and compare the paired dimensions.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#distinct_kinds_same_dimension* One dimension, two kinds.\n* 5* Try to add kinded angular frequency and frequency.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#refused_kind_addition* The kinded layer refuses cross-kind addition.\n* 6* Put the reciprocal mass/stiffness quotient under a square root in the kinded model.* HCP.L0_BlackBox#refused_reciprocal_radicand* The quotient fails before the square root: no registered edge.\n* 7* Write the L0 system context in prose.* This chapter's System-context card section* State the system boundary and assumptions before adding attributes.\n\nWorksheet: HCP/Worksheets/L0_BlackBox.lean · Solution: HCP/L0_BlackBox.lean\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L0 — The black box","header":"5.1.6. Learning path","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L0-___-The-black-box--Learning-path"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L3-___-The-body-opens-up--Questions-to-ask-the-model-so-far":{"contents":"* Question* Check* What the verdict means\n* What bears the mass of body A's left half?* opened_body* Composite.part (HalfOf .P .A) bears it; the body whole bears the assembled total.\n* Can another record of body A in pair P use the same bearer?* opened_body* Yes; it is another state, configuration, or estimate of the named system.\n* Can pair Q's left-half mass be mixed with pair P's?* opened_body* No; nominal pair identities produce distinct bearer types.\n* How does this state's centre of mass depend on its halves?* center_of_mass_mean* centerOfMassCarving uses the actual half masses; 3 at 0 and 5 at 10 yield 25/4 rather than 5. Position addition is unlicensed.\n* What happens when total mass is zero?* massless_center_of_mass* PhysLib returns the origin by convention, but hypothesis h fails, so the state cannot construct a weighted carving.\n* Does angular velocity add over a carving?* angular_velocity_intensive* No; it is intensive, and the attempted assembly is refused.\n* Can the body inertia tensor contract with lab-frame ω?* bare_frame_mismatch, framed_rotational_energy* The bare PhysLib API accepts it, but the PKC frame index refuses it.\n* Where does the homogeneous-body assumption survive?* solid_sphere* As the solid-sphere theorem (2/5) m R² · 1, ready to contribute upstream.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L3 — The body opens up","header":"5.4.9. Questions to ask the model so far","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L3-___-The-body-opens-up--Questions-to-ask-the-model-so-far"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L3-___-The-body-opens-up--Synopsis":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L3 — The body opens up","header":"5.4.1. Synopsis","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L3-___-The-body-opens-up--Synopsis"}});